# Installation
First, clone the repository:
````console
git clone https://github.com/pablovegan/riemannian-optimization-linear-optics.git
````
To run this repository in a conda environment:
````console
conda create -n env_name python==3.12 -y;
conda activate env_name
````
Once the environment is activated, install the requirements:
````console
pip install -r requirements.txt
````
To run the benchmarks, there is a separate requirements file in order to create separate conda environments:
````console
conda create -n mrm_benchmarks python==3.12 -y;
conda activate mrm_benchmarks;
pip install -r requirements_mrm.txt
````
````console
conda create -n mrm_benchmarks python==3.12 -y;
conda activate mrm_benchmarks;
pip install -r requirements_piquasso.txt
````
